+++ b/docs/acp-compaction-prototype.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Experimental ACP compaction terminal observations
+
+This increment depends on a separately reviewed, **unpublished local SDK artifact**. The default `acp` dependency remains `agent-client-protocol==0.9.0`. With that SDK, or without typed client opt-in, this increment emits no draft events and preserves the legacy initialization response.
+
+The local SDK prerequisite is `agent-client-protocol==0.9.0+ours.compaction1`, wheel `agent_client_protocol-0.9.0+ours.compaction1-py3-none-any.whl`, SHA-256 `c71ebab39ef7f779135cc93bb00bf434dcaf1740e6e54849062f9546d69d152c`. Its source patch, original manifest, deterministic builder and baseline license are in the separate review artifact at `/home/shakhvit/.hermes/acp-compaction-sdk-prototype`. This document does not designate that unpublished package as a default dependency or authorize deployment.
+
+## Isolated opt-in
+
+The reviewed SDK-only pin is `acp_adapter/compaction-sdk-requirements.txt`. To test without modifying an existing environment, use a fresh target directory and a separately provisioned test Python:
+
+```sh
+python -m pip install --no-deps --no-index --require-hashes \
+  --find-links "$ACP_COMPACTION_WHEELS" --target "$ACP_COMPACTION_TARGET" \
+  -r acp_adapter/compaction-sdk-requirements.txt
+```
+
+`ACP_COMPACTION_WHEELS` is a directory containing the reviewed wheel; `ACP_COMPACTION_TARGET` must be a disposable directory. Runtime dependencies must already be present in the test Python. The hash file does not claim to lock the complete environment.
+
+For the canonical Hermes test runner, use a test-only interpreter wrapper which exports the target directory on `PYTHONPATH`, then executes the test Python with its original arguments. Point `HERMES_PYTHON` at that wrapper. The wrapper is needed because `scripts/run_tests.sh` intentionally clears ambient environment variables. Verify `acp.__file__` and the SDK distribution version resolve to the disposable target before testing. No installation was performed in a live Hermes environment during development.
+
+## Wire contract and scope
+
+When the typed v1 `clientCapabilities.session.compaction: {}` is present, the adapter advertises the experimental metadata:
+
+```json
+{"ai.ours/compactionSafety":{"version":1,"lifecycle":"completion_only","guardedCancel":false}}
+```
+
+It emits standard draft `session/update` notifications containing only `sessionUpdate: compaction_update`, `compactionId`, and terminal `status`. No summaries, prompt bodies, checkpoint material, provider error details, or synthetic starts are included. Omitted/null client support gets no draft updates or safety metadata.
+
+A dedicated typed core callback observes local compression terminal outcomes. It reads actual commit status and cancellation state; it does not parse `compacted` status text, infer success from session rotation, or translate the legacy forced-abort completion banner into successful compaction. Each attempt has its own ID; duplicate terminals coalesce. A reporter captures its request's callback so a late worker cannot attach an old attempt to a later collector.
+
+Terminals are buffered until prompt/command finalization. Manual `/compress` temporarily suppresses the inner session DB and commits history in its outer command, so its completed terminal is released only after that command's save succeeds. Outer save failure produces failed, while the real command exception still propagates. The core records its authoritative commit result before post-commit bookkeeping, and the manual command records its outer save before token-estimate diagnostics. A later diagnostic or output failure does not rewrite an already committed compaction's result; the original exception still propagates. Observer transport errors are logged without replacing actual mutation/rollback errors.
+
+## Coverage limits
+
+This is **completion-only visibility**, with no complete start/terminal coverage or cancellation-protection promise. It does not make automatic interruption safe; Fleet must continue queueing automatic delivery until the active prompt settles.
+
+- No native Codex or Responses compaction start is fabricated. Native paths that bypass the local compression lifecycle remain unobserved by this increment.
+- Early cooldown/feasibility no-ops that never enter the local lifecycle emit no compaction entity.
+- Uninterruptible workers whose results arrive after their owning request closes do not publish into a later request. Missing outcomes are not manufactured as successful completion.
+- Events are live observations, not a durable replay/outbox or a new synchronization/control RPC.
+- The core's existing legacy human-readable status behavior remains unchanged for other hosts; only the typed observer interprets aborted admission truthfully.
+
+Tests exercise actual local automatic/manual compression mutation, provider failure, cancellation and busy-lease abort; adapter negotiation, outer persistence failure, post-commit diagnostic failure at both durable boundaries, ID deduplication, and late callback isolation. Provider calls use deterministic test responses; the real compression/facade/adapter and temporary SessionDB paths run. Draft-specific adapter tests skip when the unpinned SDK prerequisite is absent.
